@startuml
title Spec-Driven Development Flow (GitHub Spec Kit)

start

:Define Engineering Guardrails;
note right
Command:
/speckit.constitution

Purpose:
Establish non-negotiable rules:
quality, testing, security,
performance, conventions.

Artifact:
constitution.md
end note

:Define Requirements & Intent;
note right
Command:
/speckit.specify

Purpose:
Capture WHAT and WHY:
scope, requirements,
success criteria, constraints.

Artifact:
spec.md
end note

:Clarify & De-Risk Requirements;
note right
Command:
/speckit.clarify

Purpose:
Resolve ambiguity early:
edge cases, NFRs,
data & API contracts,
acceptance tests.

Artifact:
Updated spec.md
end note

:Design Technical Approach;
note right
Command:
/speckit.plan

Purpose:
Define HOW:
architecture, components,
tradeoffs, risks, rollout.

Artifact:
plan.md
end note

:Break Down Executable Work;
note right
Command:
/speckit.tasks

Purpose:
Create ordered tasks:
dependencies, deliverables,
validation steps.

Artifact:
tasks.md
end note

:Consistency & Governance Analysis;
note right
Command:
/speckit.analyze

Purpose:
Verify alignment:
- spec vs plan vs tasks
- compliance with constitution
- missing tests or constraints

Outcome:
Findings & recommendations
end note

:Readiness & Quality Checklist;
note right
Command:
/speckit.checklist

Purpose:
Pre-build quality gate:
✔ acceptance criteria
✔ test strategy
✔ security & privacy
✔ observability
✔ rollback plan
end note

if (Ready to build?) then (Yes)
  :Build & Test Solution;
  note right
Command:
/speckit.implement

Purpose:
Execute tasks,
write code & tests,
adhere to constitution.
end note

  :Validate & Deliver;
  stop
else (No)
  :Refine Spec / Plan / Tasks;
  note right
Address gaps from analyze
or checklist, then re-run
analysis & checklist.
end note
  --> :Consistency & Governance Analysis;
endif

@enduml
